<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bernardo de Gálvez</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1746–1786</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bernardo de Gálvez was a Spanish soldier who became governor of Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a> in 1777. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> entered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a>, he used <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-orleans">New Orleans</a> as a base to capture British posts in West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>, taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baton-rouge">Baton Rouge</a> in 1779, Mobile in 1780 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pensacola">Pensacola</a> in 1781. He later became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-new-spain">New Spain</a>, and Galveston in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> is named after him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bernardo-de-galvez.jpg" alt="Bernardo de Gálvez" width="320" height="435" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: José Germán de Alfaro · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Viscount_of_Galveston.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
